{:edb/db-before-t 317 :edb/db-after-t 318 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533630 50 #inst "2026-10-04T03:10:58.499Z" 13194139533630 true] [17592186087627 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242844 13194139533630 true] [17592186087627 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242847 13194139533630 true] [17592186087627 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242851 13194139533630 true] [17592186087628 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242854 13194139533630 true] [17592186087628 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242857 13194139533630 true] [17592186242844 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242845 13194139533630 true] [17592186242844 1089 "q-228897" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242844 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533630 true] [17592186242844 1100 "If ${e}^{x}=6,$ then $x≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139533630 true] [17592186242844 1113 #uuid "b2ee8216-6d1d-59ed-ad9d-e2de4dc9dea5" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242844 1138 false 13194139533630 true] [17592186242844 1145 "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x} & =6 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{x}) & =ln⁡(6) \\\\ x & =ln⁡(6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈1.792\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139533630 true] [17592186242845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242846 13194139533630 true] [17592186242845 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533630 true] [17592186242845 1041 "field-1" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242845 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242846 13194139533630 true] [17592186242845 1110 #uuid "bef023fa-665d-5288-8b1a-01eadf984860" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242846 1034 "1.792" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242846 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533630 true] [17592186242846 1111 #uuid "05d2ae20-b1e6-53c2-8203-599899848b86" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242847 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242848 13194139533630 true] [17592186242847 1089 "q-263077" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242847 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533630 true] [17592186242847 1100 "If ${e}^{3x}=9,$ then $x≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139533630 true] [17592186242847 1113 #uuid "a2647380-b90f-5a94-b8f2-387bb22f6b39" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242847 1138 false 13194139533630 true] [17592186242847 1145 "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3x} & =9 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{3x}) & =ln⁡(9) \\\\ 3x & =ln⁡(9) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}ln⁡(9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.732\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139533630 true] [17592186242848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242849 13194139533630 true] [17592186242848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242850 13194139533630 true] [17592186242848 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533630 true] [17592186242848 1041 "field-1" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242848 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242849 13194139533630 true] [17592186242848 1110 #uuid "c9c08d88-1e8e-589f-aba6-9061ff1cb5e6" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242849 1034 "0.732" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242849 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533630 true] [17592186242849 1111 #uuid "0c9a635b-aaec-5ca8-97fc-9291250a923e" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242850 1034 "2.197" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242850 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533630 true] [17592186242850 1111 #uuid "3c91e76d-c3a3-54da-ae5d-dc5e9c149d1d" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242851 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242852 13194139533630 true] [17592186242851 1089 "q-263081" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242851 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533630 true] [17592186242851 1100 "If ${e}^{5-y/2}=\\sqrt[5]{7},$ then $y≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139533630 true] [17592186242851 1113 #uuid "1d52d063-3aaf-5d01-981f-476f12121b24" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242851 1138 false 13194139533630 true] [17592186242851 1145 "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5-y/2} & =\\sqrt[5]{7} \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{5-y/2}) & =ln⁡(\\sqrt[5]{7}) \\\\ 5-\\frac{y}{2} & =ln⁡({7}^{1/5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-\\frac{y}{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(7) \\\\ -\\frac{y}{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(7)-5 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{5}ln⁡(7)+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\ny≈9.222\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139533630 true] [17592186242852 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242853 13194139533630 true] [17592186242852 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533630 true] [17592186242852 1041 "field-1" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242852 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242853 13194139533630 true] [17592186242852 1110 #uuid "9b00f4e8-2a59-5368-91a6-0a4c4194237c" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242853 1034 "9.222" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242853 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533630 true] [17592186242853 1111 #uuid "ed15ff26-098c-539f-b65f-ec0c6ef615d7" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242854 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242855 13194139533630 true] [17592186242854 1089 "q-263199" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242854 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533630 true] [17592186242854 1100 "If $9-{e}^{3-4x}=5,$ then $x≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139533630 true] [17592186242854 1113 #uuid "cba7720d-211d-5524-a5d3-66ab503bec17" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242854 1138 false 13194139533630 true] [17592186242854 1145 "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-{e}^{3-4x} & =5 \\\\ -{e}^{3-4x} & =5-9 \\\\ -{e}^{3-4x} & =-4 \\\\ {e}^{3-4x} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3-4x} & =4 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{3-4x}) & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ 3-4x & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ -4x & =ln⁡(4)-3 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{4}ln⁡(4)+\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.403\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139533630 true] [17592186242855 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242856 13194139533630 true] [17592186242855 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533630 true] [17592186242855 1041 "field-1" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242855 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242856 13194139533630 true] [17592186242855 1110 #uuid "5cf168ad-9b88-5205-8c0b-1711ce4d2696" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242856 1034 "0.403" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242856 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533630 true] [17592186242856 1111 #uuid "c530ded5-7a6d-593d-9882-8064e7270cbe" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242857 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242858 13194139533630 true] [17592186242857 1089 "q-66902" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242857 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533630 true] [17592186242857 1100 "Given that ${e}^{-5z}-6=-2,$ find the value of $z$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139533630 true] [17592186242857 1113 #uuid "3ef74d8c-cba1-50dc-af84-671391d39214" 13194139533630 true] [17592186242857 1138 false 13194139533630 true] [17592186242857 1145 "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5z}-6 & =-2 \\\\ {e}^{-5z} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5z} & =4 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{-5z}) & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ -5z & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z=-\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(4)$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nz≈-0.277\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139533630 true] [17592186242858 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242859 13194139533630 true] [17592186242858 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242860 13194139533630 true] [17592186242858 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242861 13194139533630 true] [17592186242858 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242862 13194139533630 true] [17592186242858 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242863 13194139533630 true] [17592186242858 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 1319